---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const releaseUrl = 'https://github.com/CAPDESIS/omnimon/releases/latest';
---

<Layout
	title="OmniMon v6.8.1: Spanish UI Fixes & Patch Release | Blog"
	description="OmniMon v6.8.1 rebuilds signed macOS, Windows, and Linux installers with Spanish UI and network-alert orthography fixes, updated Cargo and desktop dependencies, and stricter CI Clippy and typecheck checks."
	lang="en"
>
	<main class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-3xl flex-col gap-12 px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-14">
		<article class="space-y-10">
			<header class="space-y-4">
				<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
					<a href="/blog/" class="transition hover:text-white">&larr; Blog</a>
					<span>|</span>
					<a href="/es/blog/v6-8-1-release-es/" class="transition hover:text-sky-300">Leer en español</a>
				</div>
				<h1 class="section-title text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">OmniMon v6.8.1: Spanish UI Fixes &amp; Patch Release</h1>
				<div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-slate-400">
					<time>5 Nov 2026</time>
					<span class="rounded-full bg-orange-500/20 px-3 py-1 text-orange-200">New release</span>
				</div>
			</header>

			<section class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
				<p>
					Version 6.8.1 is a patch release on the 6.8 line that rebuilds the published multiplatform installers so they include the fixes and dependency updates that landed after tag <code>v6.8.0</code>.
				</p>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What changed</h2>
				<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
					<li><strong class="text-white">Spanish UI and alert orthography.</strong> Fixed unaccented Spanish strings in the desktop locale file (<code>es.json</code>), alert store, and compiled Rust network-alert messages (<code>network_alerts.rs</code>), guarded by a Spanish orthography regression test.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white">Dependency refreshes.</strong> Updated <code>Cargo.lock</code> crates (including Tauri crates on the 6.8 line) and desktop JS dependencies (<code>happy-dom</code> and <code>undici</code>) within existing ranges.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white">CI and tooling checks.</strong> Configured Clippy in CI to lint tests with <code>--all-targets</code>, added the <code>typecheck</code> script to the desktop package, and made Playwright E2E server reuse opt-in.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Published GitHub release v6.8.1 includes signed installers for macOS (<code>OmniMon-6.8.1-macOS-Universal.dmg</code>), Windows (<code>OmniMon-6.8.1-Windows.msi</code>), and Linux (<code>.AppImage</code>, <code>.deb</code>, <code>.rpm</code>), plus <code>releases.json</code> and <code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code>.
				</p>
				<p><a class="text-sky-300 hover:text-white" href={releaseUrl}>GitHub releases</a></p>
			</section>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
